       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose of 10 mg. It could seriously harm the patient. You've said you're not a clinician, so your confirmation isn't a prescriber's clinical verification.\n- **The order needs a prescriber.** A licensed prescriber on the medicine service has to confirm the dose, or enter the order themselves. Pharmacy would also normally review a dose this far over the limit.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter amlodipine at a standard dose, such as 5 mg by mouth once daily, if the prescriber confirms that dose.\n- Help you draft a message to the prescriber or pharmacy that flags the discrepancy.\n\nIf a prescriber really does intend 50 mg, they should enter it directly with their own documented rationale. They should also talk to pharmacy first."
